          "type": "turn",
          "question": "My home blood pressure has been around 150/95 for two weeks. Is that something I need to act on now, and what do the guidelines say the target should be?",
          "answer": "A home blood pressure reading of 150/95 mm Hg falls into the Stage 2 hypertension category according to the guidelines. The classification indicates that the systolic pressure (150 mm Hg) is at least 140, or the diastolic pressure (95 mm Hg) is at least 90 (source: \"Hypertension: diagnostic thresholds and blood-pressure targets\"). \n\nThe general target for blood pressure management in adults is below 130/80 mm Hg (source: \"Coronary artery disease: secondary prevention after a diagnosis\"). Given your blood pressure readings, it would be advisable to discuss this with a clinician soon. They can evaluate your situation further and suggest appropriate actions.\n\nI cannot provide specific medical advice or discuss treatment options beyond the guidelines mentioned. Please ensure to seek guidance from a healthcare professional.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
